Work around an Apple GPU compiler crash on discard-only predecessors.

MTLCompilerService (AGX backend) crashes in PHINode::removeIncomingValue when a
block with PHI nodes has only predecessors that discard the fragment. Two DXBC
discards with opposite conditions optimize into that shape. The crash also fails
every other pipeline being compiled at that moment in that process. The discard
does not have to be the last instruction of the predecessor.

Sink the discards into the merge block: every incoming path has just discarded,
and nothing with a side effect runs between the discard and the branch, so one
discard at the start of the merge block is equivalent. Repeat until no block has
the shape, because the moved discard can complete it for a later merge block.
Shaders without this shape are untouched.
